  "worked_solution": "First, we express our double integral as a repeated integral:      \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\u222c}_{D}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{-3}^{-1}[{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-3}^{-1}[{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{-3}^{3}\\frac{1}{{y}^{3}}[{\\int }_{0}^{3}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-3}^{-1}\\frac{1}{{y}^{3}}{[\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}]}_{0}^{3}\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-3}^{-1}\\frac{1}{{y}^{3}}(\\frac{{3}^{3}}{3}-\\frac{{0}^{3}}{3})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-3}^{-1}\\frac{9}{{y}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-3}^{-1}\\frac{9}{{y}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}y & =9{[-\\frac{1}{2{y}^{2}}]}_{-3}^{-1} \\\\  & =9(-\\frac{1}{2(-1)^{2}}+\\frac{1}{2(-3)^{2}}) \\\\  & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$",
